  {
    "source_event_id": "28051",
    "source_url": "https://ibraaz.org/whats-on/elegy-gabrielle-goliath",
    "payload": {
      "categories": [
        {
          "slug": "exhibitions",
          "title": "Exhibition"
        }
      ],
      "datesText": {
        "html": "<p>8 Oct 2026 - 17 Jan 2027</p>"
      },
      "description": "<p style=\"margin-left:0cm;\">Developed over more than a decade as a ritual performance and installation project, Gabrielle Goliath’s <i>Elegy</i> (2015–ongoing) gathers collective acts of mourning around lives and histories marked by violence, erasure and structural loss. </p><p style=\"margin-left:0cm;\"><i>Elegy</i> has evolved through multiple geographies and communities, with performative encounters staged across Johannesburg, Cape Town, São Paulo, Paris, Amsterdam, Munich and beyond. </p><p style=\"margin-left:0cm;\">The work arrives in London for a major institutional presentation, following the shocking cancellation of the South African Pavilion in Venice and its subsequent presentation as an independent exhibition at Chiesa di Sant’Antonin, with the support of Ibraaz, the Bertha Foundation and other allies.  </p><p style=\"margin-left:0cm;\">Installed in the sonic chamber of Ibraaz's Minassa, voices and moving images immerse audiences within a space of mourning, kinship and collective care. Addressing contexts of rape culture and femicide in South Africa, the genocide of Ovaherero and Nama peoples in Namibia and the ongoing devastation of Palestinian life, <i>Elegy</i> proposes mourning not as closure, but as a sustained practice of collective presence. </p>",
      "endDate": "2027-01-17T23:59:59+00:00",
      "heading": "Gabrielle Goliath",
      "id": 28051,
      "image_url": "https://ibraaz-website.imgix.net/28051/Elegy_Joan-Thabeng_Do-Disturb-Festival-Palais-de-Tokyo-Gabrielle-Goliath-Crédits-Ayka-Lux-3_2026-09-04-140714_glqr.jpg",
      "location": "Minassa",
      "slug": "elegy-gabrielle-goliath",
      "startDate": "2026-10-08T00:00:00+00:00",
      "title": "Elegy",
      "url": "https://ibraaz.org/whats-on/elegy-gabrielle-goliath"
    }
  },
  {
    "source_event_id": "28743",
    "source_url": "https://ibraaz.org/whats-on/autumn-opening",
    "payload": {
      "categories": [
        {
          "slug": "exhibitions",
          "title": "Exhibition"
        },
        {
          "slug": "library-in-residence",
          "title": "Library-in-Residence"
        }
      ],
      "datesText": {
        "html": "<p>Thu 8 Oct, 6–8pm</p>"
      },
      "description": "<p style=\"margin-left:0px;\">Join us to celebrate the opening of Ibraaz’s autumn programme of sonic and spatial interventions with Gabrielle Goliath's <a target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://ibraaz.org/whats-on/elegy-gabrielle-goliath\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><i><u>Elegy</u></i></a><i> </i>and the <a target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://ibraaz.org/whats-on/earshot-library-in-residence\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><u>Earshot Library-in-Residence</u></a>.<br /><br />Through testimony and sonic inquiry, these exhibitions explore how sound, memories and evidence are gathered and listened to. <br /><br />Also on view are Taring Padi’s <a target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://ibraaz.org/whats-on/taring-padi\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><i><u>Rakyat Pasti Menang</u></i></a> in the Majlis and Joe Namy’s <a target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://ibraaz.org/whats-on/cosmic-breath-joe-namy\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><i><u>Cosmic Breath</u></i></a> in the Musalla.  </p><p style=\"margin-left:0px;\"><strong>About Elegy: </strong> </p><p style=\"margin-left:0px;\">In the Minassa, Gabrielle Goliath’s <i>Elegy</i> gathers collective acts of mourning around lives and histories marked by violence, erasure and structural loss. Developed over more than a decade through encounters in Johannesburg, Cape Town, São Paulo, Paris and Amsterdam, the work brings together voices and moving images across eight funerary monoliths, moving between contexts including rape culture and femicide in South Africa, the genocide of Ovaherero and Nama peoples in Namibia, and the ongoing devastation of Palestinian life. <br /> <br /><strong>About Earshot-Library-in-Residence:</strong> </p><p style=\"margin-left:0px;\">In the Iqra, Earshot-Library-in-Residence brings sound not as atmosphere, but as argument. Over nine months, the space becomes a site of sonic inquiry, where recordings are interrogated and listening becomes both exercise and method. <i>From the Field</i>, a multichannel audio experience drawn from Earshot’s eco-acoustic field recordings, plays alongside three listening stations presenting <i>The Crack and the Boom</i>, <i>Authentic Audio</i> and <i>The Sonic Identikit</i>. Together, they ask not only what a sound is, but how it is heard, by whom, through which technologies, and within what social, legal and political conditions.  </p><p style=\"margin-left:0px;\"><strong>Join us between 6–8pm for the opening evening. Please RSVP to confirm your attendance.</strong></p>",
      "endDate": "2026-10-08T20:00:00+00:00",
      "heading": "Gabrielle Goliath and Earshot",
      "id": 28743,
      "image_url": "https://ibraaz-website.imgix.net/28743/Gabrielle-Earshot_image.png",
      "location": "Ibraaz",
      "slug": "autumn-opening",
      "startDate": "2026-10-08T18:00:00+00:00",
      "title": "Autumn Opening",
      "url": "https://ibraaz.org/whats-on/autumn-opening"
    }
  },
